config MICRO_OS_FS_EXT2
    bool "ext2, read-only"
    default n
    help
        Read an ext2 volume: the superblock, the group descriptors, the
        inode table, the direct and the indirect blocks and the
        directories. The reader never writes, so write, mkdir, unlink,
        chmod and chown answer "not supported". A record of ext2 keeps a
        mode, an owner and the moments of a change, so stat, statx and
        ls -l answer with what the medium holds.
